India Time Use Survey 1998-99: person-level dataset

Builds a person-level file from the NSSO pilot Time Use Survey (Schedule TUS 1.0, July 1998 to June 1999), covering Haryana, Madhya Pradesh, Gujarat, Orissa, Tamil Nadu and Meghalaya.

What the script does

build_person_dataset.py reads two of the survey's four blocks:

Block 0 and 1 — one record per household: identification plus household characteristics (size, religion, social group, land, expenditure, type of structure, disabled members).
Block 2 — one record per household member: sex, age, relation to head, marital status, education, principal activity status.

It joins them on the 11-digit household key, so every person carries the characteristics of the household they live in, and decodes the numeric survey codes into readable labels using the official NSSO code lists.

Output: output/person_level_TUS_1998.csv, 77,593 rows, 28 columns.

Running it
pip install pandas
python build_person_dataset.py

Expects TUS_1998_CSV.zip in a data/ folder next to the script. The zip is read directly, so there is no need to unpack it.

Columns
Column	Source	Notes
